# Line endings, settled once, for everybody.
#
# Without this file the repository inherits whatever `core.autocrlf` each
# machine happens to have. Ours is `true`, so a Windows checkout rewrote every
# file to CRLF while the trees that *authored* files kept LF. That is not
# cosmetic: `tests/unit/ledger/single-writer.test.ts` strips SQL comments before
# scanning the schema for banned floating-point types, and a trailing CR defeats
# the strip — so the guard fired on its own prose in a fresh clone, and passed
# in the tree that wrote the file and on Linux CI. A guard whose result depends
# on who checked it out is not a guard.
#
# `eol=lf` normalises in the repository AND in the working tree, so every
# machine sees the same bytes as CI does.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries must never be touched.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
